          "timestamp": "2026-11-05T10:10:11-07:00",
          "message": "A span edge inside a grapheme cluster stops mattering (rich-control-codes-xh4n.s60) (#554)\n\n* A span edge inside a grapheme cluster stops mattering, and nothing joins across a segment edge (rich-control-codes-xh4n.s60)\n\n* Snapped spans are the one reader of a cell's style; an edge drops every opening extender (rich-control-codes-xh4n.s60)\n\n* An edge drops only zero-cell extenders, control text is still sealed, and cluster edges are segmented once (rich-control-codes-xh4n.s60)\n\n* Edges are judged on the bytes written and only after a glyph; a cell's style reads its cluster's start (rich-control-codes-xh4n.s60)"
        }
